From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:07:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: Complexipy 9's cognitive score, with every limit
 where it was

Complexipy 9 scores cognitive complexity by more of the paper's rules than
6 did: a comprehension's for and if clauses add nothing and no longer raise
the nesting level, while an else on a loop or a try, a mixed boolean
operator sequence and a function in a recursion cycle score more.  Of the
30,221 functions scanned here, 4,526 change score, the highest is 15 either
way and none crosses a limit, so the report and the gate are read as they
were.

The function always gets a score: an ignore comment would take it out of the
report and leave a zero nobody chose to write, so it is disregarded rather
than trusted not to appear.

A comprehension therefore rests on the two metrics this project owns, NPath
for its branches and maximum nesting for its generators, and a test records
the numbers of one so that a later change to either reading is a decision
rather than a drift.
---
 docs/maintainability.md       | 10 ++++++++++
 tests/test_maintainability.py | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 tools/maintainability.py      |  5 ++++-
 3 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/maintainability.md b/docs/maintainability.md
index b639c7c5..5c002117 100644
--- a/docs/maintainability.md
+++ b/docs/maintainability.md
@@ -51,6 +51,16 @@ comes from [Complexipy](https://github.com/rohaquinlop/complexipy). The project
 owns the two short AST implementations for NPath and nesting so their behavior
 is inspectable and covered by unit tests.
 
+Complexipy 9 reads a comprehension as shorthand for a loop, so its `for` and
+`if` clauses add nothing to the cognitive score and a nested comprehension can
+score zero. That is the library's reading of the paper, not a hole in this
+gate: the project's own two metrics still count a comprehension, NPath for its
+branches and maximum nesting for its generators, so a comprehension deep enough
+to be hard to read is held back by those. Cognitive Complexity is reported as
+Complexipy measures it, never adjusted here, and
+`test_a_comprehension_is_gated_by_paths_and_nesting_rather_than_cognitive`
+records the numbers for one.
+
 This project's NPath calculation multiplies independent sequential choices and
 adds mutually exclusive alternatives. It includes short-circuit Boolean
 expressions, conditional expressions, loop termination, exception handlers,
diff --git a/tests/test_maintainability.py b/tests/test_maintainability.py
index dd1f5e51..8403f041 100644
--- a/tests/test_maintainability.py
+++ b/tests/test_maintainability.py
@@ -34,6 +34,25 @@ def choices(x):
     assert measured.max_nesting == 3
 
 
+def test_a_comprehension_is_gated_by_paths_and_nesting_rather_than_cognitive() -> None:
+    """Complexipy reads a comprehension as shorthand for a loop, so it adds no
+    cognitive score: a twice-nested one with a condition scores zero. The
+    project's own two metrics still count it, which is what holds such a
+    function back when it is nested too deeply to read."""
+    source = """
+def labels(rows):
+    return ["".join(shade(cell) for cell in row if cell) for row in rows if row]
+"""
+
+    (measured,) = mt.analyze_source(source, "comprehension.py")
+
+    assert measured.key == "comprehension.py::labels"
+    assert measured.cognitive == 0
+    assert measured.ccn == 5
+    assert measured.npath == 16
+    assert measured.max_nesting == 2
+
+
 def test_npath_multiplies_independent_branches() -> None:
     node = _function(
         """
diff --git a/tools/maintainability.py b/tools/maintainability.py
index 7bfaeeb9..1bf29038 100644
--- a/tools/maintainability.py
+++ b/tools/maintainability.py
@@ -312,7 +312,10 @@ def _library_metrics(node: ast.AST) -> tuple[int, int, float]:
     cyclomatic_blocks = cc_visit_ast(module)
     ccn = cyclomatic_blocks[0].complexity
 
-    cognitive_report = code_complexity(ast.unparse(module))
+    # The function's score is always reported: an ignore comment would take it
+    # out of the report and leave a zero nobody chose to write.  The source is
+    # unparsed and carries none, which the flag makes a rule rather than a hope.
+    cognitive_report = code_complexity(ast.unparse(module), no_ignore=True)
     cognitive = cognitive_report.functions[0].complexity
 
     halstead_report = h_visit_ast(module)
